the role of Metropolitan Police  Commissioner is the biggest in UK  policing but what does the job involve  the commissioner is chosen by the Home  Secretary but the views of the mayor of  London have to be taken into account the  commissioner's main job is to run the  police in London but it comes with some  national responsibilities too the  commissioner commands nearly 34 000  police officers at around 10 000 support  staff it takes a lot of people and  resources to try to keep the capitals  nine million people safe  the Mets National role includes  counter-terrorism guarding the royal  family Parliament and Senior politicians  and protecting foreign embassies  Kitchener and the Met are independent of  government but a tricky part of the job  is managing the tensions and  expectations of two bosses who may be  from opposing political parties  the last commissioner Dane Cressida dick  resigned after clashing with Labor's  London mayor Sadiq Khan though she  appeared to have the support of the Tory  Home Secretary putty Patel  public trust and confidence in the Met  police fell after a wave of scandals  during Crescent addict's time as  commissioner they included the abduction  rape and murder of marketing executive  Sarah everard by off-duty PC Wayne  cousins the taking and sharing of  photographs of two murdered Sisters by  police guarding their bodies  the racist and misogynist text message  sharing by officers at Charing Cross  police station  the forces handling of lockdown parties  in Downing Street  and the strip searching of a young black  schoolgirl in East London  [Music]  replacing Dame Cressida dick is Sir Mark  Rowley  promise more trust less crime and high  standards I will to the best of my skill  and knowledge discharge all duties  thereof faithfully and according to the  law he was an assistant commissioner at  the Met and head of counter-terror  policing for the UK between 2014 and  2018 he was knighted for his services to  policing and was also awarded the  Queen's police medal  before that he was the chief Constable  of Surrey and spent five years leading  the high-profile investigation into the  murder of Millie Dowler  he admits some friends thought he was  crazy to take on his new job samark will  be under No Illusion about the  improvements he's expected to make in  the Mets culture and performance and his  political Masters will want results soon
 

